# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values.
#   cp .env.example .env.local
# Never commit .env.local (it's in .gitignore) — it contains your API key.

# ===== Ollama (Member 2 — AI module) =====
# Local Ollama server (default):
#   OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434   → no key needed
# Ollama Cloud (hosted inference):
#   OLLAMA_HOST=https://ollama.com       → requires OLLAMA_API_KEY below
OLLAMA_HOST=https://ollama.com

# API key from https://ollama.com/settings/keys (only needed for cloud).
# Leave empty for local Ollama.
# OLLAMA_API_KEY=

# Model used for recommendations.
# Local:   pull it first (e.g. `ollama pull llama3.1`).
# Cloud:   any model on your account, WITHOUT the `-cloud` suffix
#          (e.g. gemma4:31b, glm-5.3-flash, kimi-k2.6, gpt-oss:120b).
OLLAMA_MODEL=gemma4:31b

# ===== Rate limiting (Member 2 — in-memory, per IP, per process) =====
# Max tokens (requests) a client can burst before being throttled
RATE_LIMIT_MAX=30
# How many tokens refill per minute
RATE_LIMIT_REFILL_PER_MINUTE=15

# ===== Database (Postgres via Prisma) =====
# Everything the app stores — accounts, profiles, chat sessions, and the
# generated career maps — lives here.
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT (docker-compose.yml)
#   1. Copy the POSTGRES_* lines below into a file called `.env`
#      (docker compose reads `.env`, Next.js reads `.env.local` — both gitignored)
#   2. npm run db:up        start Postgres and wait until it's healthy
#   3. npm run db:migrate   apply the migrations
#   4. npm run db:studio    optional: browse the data
#
#   The container keeps its data in the `careercompass-data` volume, so
#   `npm run db:down` then `npm run db:up` loses nothing. To start over
#   completely: docker compose down -v
#
#   Note: POSTGRES_* is only read when the volume is first created. Changing
#   the password afterwards has no effect on an existing volume.
POSTGRES_USER=career
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=pick-something-local
POSTGRES_DB=careercompass

# The connection string the app itself uses. Keep it in .env.local.
# Local:  postgresql://career:pick-something-local@localhost:5432/careercompass
#
# DEPLOYED (Vercel): a local container is unreachable from serverless functions,
# so production needs a HOSTED Postgres — Neon, Vercel Postgres or Supabase all
# have free tiers. Paste that connection string here instead, keeping
# `?sslmode=require` if the provider includes it. Then run `npm run db:migrate`
# against it.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://career:CHANGE_ME@localhost:5432/careercompass

# ===== Deploying to Vercel =====
# Set these in the Vercel project (Settings → Environment Variables), not here.
#
#   DATABASE_URL    a HOSTED Postgres. A local container is unreachable from
#                   serverless functions — `localhost:5432` means nothing from
#                   Vercel's network. Neon / Vercel Postgres / Supabase all have
#                   free tiers.
#   OLLAMA_API_KEY  required for BOTH chat and web search. Without it the app
#                   boots but every turn fails.
#   OLLAMA_MODEL    e.g. gemma4:31b
#   OLLAMA_HOST     https://ollama.com
#
# Then apply the schema to that database once:
#   DATABASE_URL=<hosted-url> npx prisma migrate deploy
#
# Serverless connection pooling: each function instance opens its own pool, so
# prefer your provider's POOLED connection string (Neon's `-pooler` host,
# Supabase's port 6543). If you see "too many clients already", that's what it
# is. Migrations sometimes fail over a pooler — if `prisma migrate deploy`
# errors, add a `directUrl` to the datasource in prisma/schema.prisma pointing
# at the non-pooled URL.
#
# After deploying, GET /api/health reports what's misconfigured, if anything.
#
# Two known platform limits:
#   - /api/chat declares maxDuration = 60 because a research turn takes ~30-40s.
#     Hobby's default is 10s, which would kill the stream. 60 is Hobby's ceiling.
#   - The rate limiter in lib/rateLimit.ts keeps counters in memory, so each
#     serverless instance enforces its own. It is not a global limit in production.

# ===== Web tools (web_search / web_fetch) =====
# These are Ollama's own hosted endpoints (https://ollama.com/api/web_search
# and /api/web_fetch). They are the ONLY search/fetch provider used — there are
# no Tavily/SerpAPI/Brave keys to configure any more.
#
# They need OLLAMA_API_KEY above, even if OLLAMA_HOST points at a local server,
# because the SDK always posts these two calls to ollama.com.
# Get a key at https://ollama.com/settings/keys
#
# Optional tuning (see lib/tools/index.ts for the full list):
#   results per search are clamped to 5; every result link is fetched and then
#   summarized by one extra model call so raw pages never reach the chat context.
